    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d829">

                <pb facs="0773" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.74/9–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-29T20:00:00+03:00">September 29,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—10:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2931. From Eddy.<anchor n="93" xml:id="d829-f1"/> Reliable confidential source
                    informs me London has replied (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) objecting to a
                    Saudi Government radio station and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) asking that
                    their objection be kept secret. Since notice to terminate monopoly of Eastern
                    Telegraph must antedate December 1, I recommend following immediate steps.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department request from British Government “no objection” to Saudi
                        Government radio station for communication with countries not served by
                        Eastern Telegraph, including the United States of America.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Legation Jidda be instructed to ask Saudi Government whether they have
                        London reply and whether they plan radio station.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed> [Eddy] <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d829-f1" n="93" xml:id="d829-f1-content">
                <p>William A. Eddy, Minister in Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
